From 93fc93bf789c3b94faf5efff69e6073290fe505e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "servicemp3 gst-1.26 review" <noreply@example.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 13:13:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] servicemp3: fix inverted stream-list change detection

In the ASYNC_DONE handler the check whether the audio/subtitle stream
lists changed used std::equal() without negation:

  hasChanges = size differs || std::equal(old, new)

so an unchanged list was reported as changed (re-enumeration and a
spurious evUpdatedInfo on every ASYNC_DONE, e.g. after each seek),
while a list with the same number of streams but different
language/codec was reported as unchanged and never refreshed.

Verified with the real eServiceMP3::audioStream struct: of three
scenarios (unchanged / same count but different content / different
count) the old expression decides two wrongly, the new one none.

Behavioural note: evUpdatedInfo is no longer emitted on every
ASYNC_DONE, only when the stream lists really change.
---
 servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp b/servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp
index 8ba703c..0c2a92a 100644
--- a/servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp
+++ b/servicemp3/servicemp3.cpp
@@ -2227,9 +2227,9 @@ void eServiceMP3::gstBusCall(GstMessage *msg)
 				subtitleStreams_temp.push_back(subs);
 			}
 
-			bool hasChanges = m_audioStreams.size() != audioStreams_temp.size() || std::equal(m_audioStreams.begin(), m_audioStreams.end(), audioStreams_temp.begin());
+			bool hasChanges = m_audioStreams.size() != audioStreams_temp.size() || !std::equal(m_audioStreams.begin(), m_audioStreams.end(), audioStreams_temp.begin());
 			if (!hasChanges)
-				hasChanges = m_subtitleStreams.size() != subtitleStreams_temp.size() || std::equal(m_subtitleStreams.begin(), m_subtitleStreams.end(), subtitleStreams_temp.begin());
+				hasChanges = m_subtitleStreams.size() != subtitleStreams_temp.size() || !std::equal(m_subtitleStreams.begin(), m_subtitleStreams.end(), subtitleStreams_temp.begin());
 
 			if (hasChanges)
 			{
